WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.354
Chapter 11. Read-only Web MCP and local MCP boundaries. Web MCP exposes only fixed resources, read-only analysis, and the download manifest. It offers no arbitrary URL, file, command, or credential access. The local Python MCP and Cloudflare Pages Function are separate transports with different protocol versions and body limits.

2
00:00:28.674 --> 00:00:58.042
The Cloudflare Pages Function uses POST /api/mcp, protocol 2025-03-26, a 32 KiB body cap, and a default 60 requests per minute per source IP. Public binding requires MI_MCP_PUBLIC_TOKEN of at least 32 characters in deployment secrets; MI_MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS is an exact Origin allowlist.

3
00:00:58.362 --> 00:01:32.554
Web tools include meaning_analyze, meaning_review, resource_catalog, evidence_levels, and download_manifest. Resources include mi://canon/v7, mi://evidence/e0-e6, mi://chapters/zh, mi://chapters/en, mi://skills/l1-l6, and mi://downloads. URIs are virtual identifiers, not filesystem paths.

4
00:01:32.874 --> 00:02:00.683
The local Python MCP defaults to 127.0.0.1:8767, protocol 2024-11-05, and a 512 KiB core request cap; its public transport policy also defaults to loopback. Non-loopback binding requires a strong token. Both remain read-only. This guide did not access or read credentials.

5
00:02:01.003 --> 00:02:13.295
Web: POST /api/mcp; 2025-03-26; 32 KiB.

6
00:02:13.615 --> 00:02:28.817
Local MCP: 127.0.0.1:8767; 2024-11-05; 512 KiB.

7
00:02:29.137 --> 00:02:39.789
Read-only: fixed resources, analysis, review, download manifest.

8
00:02:40.109 --> 00:02:50.632
Forbidden: arbitrary URLs, paths, shell, credential reads.

9
00:02:50.952 --> 00:03:08.888
Try one step: In an authorized test environment, verify unauthorized rejection, tools/list, resources/read, and both read-only tools. Never write a test token to logs or documents.

10
00:03:09.208 --> 00:03:29.073
Pending verification: Local focused tests do not replace production acceptance. The release owner must verify the public token, Origin allowlist, rate limits, headers, and authorized calls in an authorized environment and record them in the external deployment report.
